body: "pm-cli now uses pm-changelog for the main CHANGELOG.md. The generated current-release section uses headings like `## 2026.5.24 - 2026-05-24`, while the existing released changelog follows Keep a Changelog style headings like `## [2026.5.24] - 2026-05-24` and includes older release sections.\\n\\nWhen pm-cli switches from destructive `--mode replace` to the safer package-owned `--mode prepend`, pm-changelog fails to identify those headings as the same release. It inserts a duplicate current-release section instead of replacing the existing section, so projects cannot preserve real release history while regenerating the current release from pm items.\\n\\nExpected behavior:\\n- `mergeChangelog` / `--mode prepend` should treat bracketed Keep a Changelog headings as equivalent to unbracketed generated headings for the same version.\\n- Example: generated `## 2026.5.24 - 2026-05-24` should replace existing `## [2026.5.24] - 2026-05-24`.\\n- Older release sections and top-of-file prose should be preserved.\\n\\nThis is needed so pm-cli can rely on pm-changelog without custom scripts or hand-written changelog repair.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-05-24T14:20:02Z)\n>\n> Fixed in pm-changelog and published as npm latest 2026.5.24-11. The fix normalizes generated and Keep a Changelog bracketed release headings in prepend mode, and the release workflow now uses prepend mode so older sections are preserved."
